:: Robin Bunny
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
While you're beside Robin, you suddenly feel like bumping your head against <<him>>. You turn and gently bump your forehead against <<him>>.
<<if $robin.timer.hurt gte 1>>
Robin pauses, then places a hand against your head and moves you away. <<He>> still seems uncomfortable being touched.
<<else>>
As you move closer, your ears brush Robin's nose and <<he>> starts giggling.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Water Dragon
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
You relax beside Robin while <<he>> plays <<his>> game. Your tail begins to wag, and you make little squeaks and short, sharp noises from your throat without meaning to.
Robin stops playing and looks over. "You sound like a dolphin!" <<he>> says with a giggle, making you laugh too.
<br><br>
<<He>> tries making the same noise. The first attempt sounds nothing like yours, so you do it again for <<him>> to copy. You take turns until Robin can almost make the same sound, laughing together whenever <<he>> gets it wrong.
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Talk Transgender
<<endevent>><<effects>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<set _identity to playerFeltGender()>><<set _correction to $robinGenderTalk is 1>>
<<if _correction>>
	<<set $robinGenderTalk to 2>>
<<else>>
	<<set $robinGenderTalk to _identity is "n" ? 1 : 2>><<run $transgenderknown.pushUnique("Robin")>>
<</if>>
<<if _correction>>
	Robin pauses <<his>> game when you sit down. "What's wrong?"
	<br><br>
	You explain that <<he>> misunderstood you. You said your body was not the problem, but Robin decided that must mean you wanted to be the opposite gender. <<He>> never asked what you actually meant.
	<br><br>
	"Oh." <<He>> sets the controller down. "I thought that was what you meant."
<<else>>
	Robin pauses <<his>> game when you sit down. "What's wrong?"
	<br><br>
	You tell Robin that people decide whether you're a boy or a girl just by looking at your body. When you dress in clothes that feel right to you, some people call it crossdressing, as if you're only pretending to be someone else. That's what hurts.
	<br><br>
	Robin sets the controller down. "So you want to be a <<if _identity is "f" or (_identity is "n" and playerOriginalSex() is "m")>>girl<<else>>boy<</if>>," <<he>> says.
	"That's what it means, right?"
	<<if _identity is "n">><br><br>Robin doesn't sound unkind, but <<he>> has misunderstood you.<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _identity is "f">>
	"I'm a girl," you say. "Not becoming one. I already am."
	<br><br>
	Robin takes a moment with that.
<<elseif _identity is "m">>
	"I'm a boy," you say. "Not becoming one. I already am."
	<br><br>
	Robin takes a moment with that.
<<else>>
	"I'm not a boy or a girl," you say. "Not one hiding as the other. Neither."
	<br><br>
	Robin frowns. "But there's got to be one that fits better."
	<br><br>
	"There isn't."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> doesn't argue, but <<he>> doesn't look like <<he>> follows either.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Okay," <<he>> says. "Can I ask you something? I might ask it badly."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Talk Transgender Body]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Talk Transgender Body
<<effects>>
Robin goes quiet for a few moments, trying to decide how to ask <<his>> next question.
<br><br>
"There are pills that change you," <<he>> says. "Everyone at school knows someone who's taken one.
<<if $xchange.pill.active>>Has taking one helped? With feeling at home in your body, I mean?"
<<else>>If you took one and woke up in a body that matched, would that fix it?"<</if>>
<br><br>
You think about <<his>> question before answering.
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.pill.active>>
	<<link [[Yes. It helps|Robin Talk Transgender End]]>><<set $robinGenderTalkBody to "yes">><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Yes. I'd take it tonight|Robin Talk Transgender End]]>><<set $robinGenderTalkBody to "yes">><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[My body isn't what's wrong|Robin Talk Transgender End]]>><<set $robinGenderTalkBody to "no">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[I don't know|Robin Talk Transgender End]]>><<set $robinGenderTalkBody to "unsure">><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Talk Transgender End
<<effects>>
<<set _identity to playerFeltGender()>>
<<if $robinGenderTalkBody is "yes">>
	You tell Robin yes right away. You know how you feel about your body, even if you don't want to explain everything.
	<br><br>
	<<if $xchange.pill.active>>
		"I'm glad it helps," Robin says. "I didn't know."
	<<else>>
		"Then I hope you get one," Robin says. "A good one, not the ones people hand out at parties."
	<</if>>
<<elseif $robinGenderTalkBody is "no">>
	You tell Robin no. You aren't asking for a different body. The problem is that other people look at your body and decide your gender without listening to you.
	<br><br>
	Robin nods slowly. "So a pill wouldn't stop them. It'd just change what they decided about you."
	<br><br>
	"That's it," you say.
<<else>>
	You admit you don't know what would help yet. Having to think about it all the time is tiring too.
	<br><br>
	"That's allowed," Robin says. "You don't have to have it worked out to be right about it."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<Hes>> quiet for a while. When <<he>> speaks again <<hes>> looking at the floor.
"Bailey decides what I am. What I wear, what I'm for, what I'm called when there's money in it.
The kids at school do it too. I've never once been asked."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks up at you. "I know a bit of what that's like. Not what you're going through specifically...
just what it feels like when everyone else tries to decide who you are."
<br><br>
Robin rarely talks this much about how Bailey or the other students treat <<him>>. <<He>> reaches for your hand and waits until you look at <<him>> before speaking again.
<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 70>>
	"I'll call you whatever you want me to. And if someone gives you trouble about it, tell me."
	<br><br>
	You raise an eyebrow. Robin quickly adds, "So I can help. I don't mean I get to decide anything for you."
<<else>>
	"I'll use the words you tell me to use," <<he>> says. "And please correct me if I get something wrong. I'd rather you told me."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _identity is "n">>
	Robin hesitates, then gives your hand a small squeeze. The uncertainty remains on <<his>> face,
	but <<he>> stays beside you without pulling away.
<</if>>
Eventually <<he>> picks the controller back up and lets you stay beside <<him>> while <<he>> plays.
<<stress -6>><<lstress>><<npcincr Robin love 3>><<glove>><<npcincr Robin dom 2>><<gdom>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Gender Reminder
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<set $daily.robin.genderReminder to 1>>
<<if $robinGenderReminders is undefined>><<set $robinGenderReminders to 0>><</if>>
While you're talking, Robin uses the wrong word for your gender again. <<He>> carries on speaking without realising what <<he>> said.
<br><br>
<<link [[Correct <<him>>|Robin Gender Reminder Soft]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> to stop|Robin Gender Reminder Firm]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Let it go|Robin Gender Reminder Ignore]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Gender Reminder Soft
<<effects>>
<<set $robinGenderReminders++>>
<<set _count to $robinGenderReminders>>
You say the correct word quietly so Robin knows what <<he>> got wrong, without stopping the whole conversation.
<br><br>
<<if _count lte 2>>
	Robin winces. "Which part did I get wrong?" <<he>> asks. After you tell <<him>>,
	<<he>> repeats what <<he>> meant to say, using the right word this time.
	<<npcincr Robin dom 1>><<gdom>><<stress -3>><<lstress>>
<<elseif _count lte 5>>
	Robin lowers <<his>> head and hunches slightly. "Sorry... Which part did I get wrong?"
	<br><br>
	You tell <<him>>, and <<he>> nods before starting the sentence again, using the right word this time.
	<<He>> speaks more carefully now, pausing when <<hes>> unsure rather than guessing.
	<<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<ldom>><<stress -2>><<lstress>>
<<else>>
	Robin flinches and looks down. "Sorry. What did I say wrong?" <<he>> asks.
	<<He>> waits for you to explain before trying again.
	<br><br>
	<<Hes>> so afraid of hurting you again that <<he>> starts questioning every word before <<he>> says it.
	<<He>> uses the right words now, but often stays quiet when <<hes>> unsure.
	<<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<ldom>><<npcincr Robin trauma 1>><<grtrauma>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Gender Reminder Firm
<<effects>>
<<set $robinGenderReminders++>>
<<set _count to $robinGenderReminders>>
You tell <<him>> firmly, "Stop calling me that."
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 70>>
    Robin stops speaking and looks directly at you.
	"Right," <<he>> says, nodding quickly. "I'm sorry. That's my fault."
    <br><br>
    <<He>> starts to say something else, then decides not to. <<He>> looks away, worried about getting it wrong again.
    <<npcincr Robin dom -2>><<ldom>>
<<else>>
    Robin stops moving and stares at you, suddenly worried. "Sorry! I'm so sorry, I wasn't thinking..."
    <br><br>
    <<He>> pulls back, looking nervous. Over the next few minutes, <<he>> keeps apologising,
	even for things that have nothing to do with what happened. <<He>> seems worried that you're still angry with <<him>>.
    <<npcincr Robin dom -2>><<ldom>><<npcincr Robin trauma 2>><<grtrauma>>
<</if>>
<<if _count gte 4>>
    <br><br>
    <<Hes>> getting the words right more often now, but <<he>> still looks nervous whenever the subject comes up.
	After each sentence, <<he>> glances at your face before continuing,
	as though checking whether <<he>> said something wrong.
	<br><br>
	You've seen <<him>> act like this around Bailey when <<he>> expects to be punished.
    <<npcincr Robin love -1>><<llove>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Gender Reminder Ignore
<<effects>>
You notice the mistake but decide not to correct Robin this time. <<He>> continues talking without knowing anything is wrong.
<br><br>
<<if $robinGenderReminders gte 3>>
    You've corrected Robin several times already, and you're tired of having to do it. For now, staying quiet feels easier.
<<else>>
    Even after the conversation moves on, you wish you'd said something.
    <<stress 3>><<gstress>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Outfit Offer
<!-- $location is still the passage you came from: the cafe, the stand, or Robin's room. Keep it. -->
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _outfitVenue to ["cafe", "park", "beach"].includes($location) ? $location : "home">><<set $location to _outfitVenue>><<effects>>
<<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set _reaction to robinOutfitReaction($pocket.outfit.pieces)>>
<!-- The outcome passages need this after the bundle has left the player's hands. Cleared on the way out. -->
<<set $robinOutfitPending to {
	verdict: _reaction.verdict,
	reason: _reaction.reason,
	crossdress: _reaction.crossdress,
	sexy: _reaction.sexy,
	modest: _reaction.modest,
	name: pocketOutfitName(),
	list: pocketOutfitPieceNames()
}>>
You take out the clothes you've brought for Robin and hand them over. <<He>> pulls back a fold of fabric to see what's inside. "Is this—"
<br><br>
When <<he>> unfolds the <<= $robinOutfitPending.name>>, <<he>> realises it's an outfit for <<him>>. <<He>> holds it against <<his>> body to imagine how it would look when worn, then lowers it when <<he>> notices you watching. <<His>> face turns red.
<<if $robinOutfitPending.list.length gt 1>>
	<br><br>
	There are more pieces underneath: <<= $robinOutfitPending.list.slice(1).join(", ")>>.
	Robin takes them out one by one, looking at each piece before deciding what to say.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $robinOutfitPending.verdict is "refuse">>
	<<link [[Wait for <<him>> to say something|Robin Outfit Refuse]]>><</link>>
<<elseif $robinOutfitPending.verdict is "keep">>
	<<link [[Wait for <<him>> to say something|Robin Outfit Keep]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Wait for <<him>> to say something|Robin Outfit Accept]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Robin Outfit Refuse
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<if ndef $robinOutfitPending>><<run robinOutfitPendingRebuild()>><</if>>
<<if $robinOutfitPending.reason is "trauma">>
	<<His>> hands stop over the clothes. After looking at them for a few seconds, <<he>> folds each piece and puts the bundle back into your hands.
	<br><br>
	"Not now," <<he>> says. "Please."<<npcincr Robin trauma 1>><<grtrauma>>
	<br><br>
	Robin is <span class="blue">too distressed</span> to consider wearing the outfit. You keep it.
<<else>>
	<<He>> looks over the <<= $robinOutfitPending.name>> again. <<Hes>> about to unfold it when <<he>> realises what wearing it would mean, and <<his>> hands stop.
	<br><br>
	"It's... that's a <<print $robinOutfitPending.crossdress ? "girl's" : "boy's">> one," <<he>> says.
	<<He>> lowers the outfit and looks down at it. "I've never worn anything like this. Not even when I'm alone.
	I wouldn't know how to start."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> folds it again and puts it back into your hands.
	Afterwards, <<he>> keeps looking down at the clothes instead of at you.
	<br><br>
	Robin <span class="blue">isn't ready</span> to wear something like that. You keep the outfit.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinOutfitReturn>>

:: Robin Outfit Keep
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<if ndef $robinOutfitPending>><<run robinOutfitPendingRebuild()>><</if>>
<<if $robinOutfitPending.sexy>>
	<<He>> opens the outfit fully and holds it up. When <<he>> sees how much skin it would leave uncovered, <<he>> quickly lowers it and folds part of the fabric over again.
	<br><br>
	"People would <i>look</i>," <<he>> says, staring at it with a red face.
<<elseif $robinOutfitPending.crossdress>>
	<<He>> holds the outfit against <<his>> body again, then glances around.
	<br><br>
	"I could wear it," <<he>> says, lowering <<his>> voice. "But only in my room, with the door shut. I don't think I could wear it outside yet."
<<else>>
	Robin runs <<his>> thumb over one of the places where the fabric is sewn together. "It's really nice. Like the uniforms at those expensive places."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Robin folds the pieces together, careful not to lose any of them.
<<if $location is "home">>
	<<He>> puts the outfit in <<his>> drawer, where Bailey is unlikely to find it, and closes the drawer.
<<else>>
	<<He>> keeps the folded outfit with <<him>>. "I'll hide it from Bailey when I get home," <<he>> says.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Thank you. Really," Robin says, looking at the outfit once more. "I don't think I can wear it at work yet. Ask me again sometime?"
<<npcincr Robin love 2>><<npcincr Robin trauma -2>><<gglove>><<lrtrauma>>
<br><br>
<span class="blue">Ask again</span> when Robin has more confidence<<if $robinOutfitPending.crossdress>>, and is comfortable crossdressing where people can see<</if>>.
<<run robinOutfitAccept(false)>>
<br><br>
<<robinOutfitReturn>>

:: Robin Outfit Accept
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<if ndef $robinOutfitPending>><<run robinOutfitPendingRebuild()>><</if>>
<<if $robinOutfitPending.sexy and $robinOutfitPending.crossdress>>
	<<He>> opens the outfit fully and holds it against <<his>> body again.
	This time, <<he>> keeps it there while looking down at it.
	<br><br>
	"You bought this for me," <<he>> says. <<His>> face turns red, but <<he>> starts smiling.
	"You actually bought <i>this</i> one."<<npcincr Robin lust 6>><<gglust>>
<<elseif $robinOutfitPending.sexy>>
	<<He>> turns the outfit around to look at the front and back.
	<<His>> face turns pink when <<he>> sees how revealing it is.
	<br><br>
	"Sam is definitely going to say something about this," <<he>> says. <<He>> looks at the outfit again.
	"That's fine. I'm still wearing it."<<npcincr Robin lust 3>><<glust>>
<<elseif $robinOutfitPending.crossdress>>
	<<He>> looks down at the outfit, then towards the door before turning back to you.
	<br><br>
	"At <i>work</i>?" <<he>> asks. <<His>> face turns red as <<he>> looks down at the clothes again.
	"Where everyone can see me wearing it?"
	<br><br>
	You start to answer, but <<he>> takes a breath and lifts the outfit again.
	"Yes," <<he>> says. "Okay. I'll do it."<<npcincr Robin lust 2>><<glust>>
<<else>>
	<<He>> holds the outfit against <<his>> body again and smooths the front with one hand.
	<br><br>
	"This is a real uniform," <<he>> says. "And it's mine. I won't have to borrow an apron anymore."
<</if>>
<<npcincr Robin love 2>><<gglove>>
<br><br>
Robin looks at the clothes again, then starts talking about when <<he>> could wear them. <<He>> wonders which shift would be best and whether Sam will mind. <<He>> also asks how the outfit should be washed so it won't get damaged.
<<run robinOutfitAccept(true)>>
<br><br>
<<robinOutfitReturn>>

:: Robin Outfit Wear
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _outfitVenue to ["cafe", "park", "beach"].includes($location) ? $location : "home">><<set $location to _outfitVenue>><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<!-- Reaching an outfit scene without the outfit (an old save, the debug menu) degrades instead of throwing.
The <<exit>> has to be here rather than in a widget: inside a widget it only ends the widget. -->
<<if !$robinCafe.outfit>>
	Robin doesn't have anything of yours to wear.
	<br><br>
	<<robinOutfitReturn>>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
<<set $robinCafe.outfit.worn to true>>
You ask Robin if <<he>> still has the <<= $robinCafe.outfit.name>>.
<br><br>
"You remembered," Robin says with a smile.
<<if $location is "home">>
	<<He>> opens <<his>> drawer and takes out the outfit. <<He>> has kept it folded, but the fabric still has lines where it was stored. <<He>> unfolds it across the bed so you can both see it.
<<else>>
	"It's still at home, in my drawer," <<he>> says. <<He>> glances at you before continuing.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"I've looked at it a few times," <<he>> admits. "I kept thinking about wearing it, then deciding I wasn't ready."
<br><br>
<<if $robinCafe.outfit.crossdress>>
	"I tried it on too, but only in my room," Robin says. "I thought I'd want to take it off straight away. But I didn't want to take it off."
<<elseif $robinCafe.outfit.sexy>>
	"I kept telling myself I'd wear it. Then I'd look at it and change my mind."
	<<if $location is "home">>
		<<He>> picks up the outfit and holds it against <<his>> body again. This time, <<he>> doesn't quickly put it away.
	<<else>>
		<<He>> smiles at you, then looks away. "I think I could manage it now, though."
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	"I wanted to wear it, but I kept wondering if I should," <<he>> admits. "I think I wanted someone else to tell me it was okay."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Outfit Wear 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Outfit Wear 2
<<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<if !$robinCafe.outfit>>
	Robin doesn't have anything of yours to wear.
	<br><br>
	<<robinOutfitReturn>>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
Robin nods to <<himself>> as <<he>> makes up <<his>> mind.
<<if $location is "home">>
	<<He>> folds the outfit and holds it over <<his>> arm.
<</if>>
"Tomorrow. Yes. I'll wear it tomorrow, before I change my mind again."
<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<npcincr Robin dom 3>><<glove>><<ggdom>>
<br><br>
<i>Robin will wear the <<= $robinCafe.outfit.name>> <span class="gold">during <<his>> next shift</span>.</i>
<br><br>
<<robinOutfitReturn>>

:: Robin Outfit Debut
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<!-- Reaching an outfit scene without the outfit (an old save, the debug menu) degrades instead of throwing.
The <<exit>> has to be here rather than in a widget: inside a widget it only ends the widget. -->
<<if !$robinCafe.outfit>>
	Robin doesn't have anything of yours to wear.
	<br><br>
	<<robinOutfitReturn>>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
<<robinOutfitLook>>
<<set $robinCafe.outfit.seen.debut to true>>
When you enter the café, you notice several customers watching Robin instead of talking to each other. <<Hes>> carrying a tray with three plates of food towards one of the tables.
<br><br>
Robin watches the tray carefully as <<he>> walks between the chairs. <<He>> avoids looking back at the customers, even when some of them turn to watch <<him>> pass.
<br><br>
<<if $robinCafe.outfit.crossdress and $robinCafe.outfit.sexy>>
	Two regulars by the window stop talking when Robin passes them.
	Sam stays behind the coffee machine and keeps working without looking over.
	<br><br>
	Robin puts the three plates on the table and brings the empty tray back to the counter. After setting it down, <<he>> puts both hands on the counter and looks at you.
	"Don't say anything about the outfit."
	<br><br>
	"I wasn't going to." You shrug.
	<br><br>
	Robin looks away. "You were still thinking about it."<<npcincr Robin lust 3>><<glust>>
<<elseif $robinCafe.outfit.sexy>>
	One of the regulars by the window leans towards their friend and says something quietly while watching Robin.
	Robin hears them. <<His>> ears turn red, but <<he>> keeps carrying the order to the table.
	<br><br>
	After serving the food, <<he>> comes back with the empty tray and sets it on the counter.
	"That's the third person who's commented on the outfit. I've been counting."
	<<npcincr Robin lust 2>><<glust>>
<<elseif $robinCafe.outfit.crossdress>>
	People look at Robin when <<he>> walks past, but nobody says anything about <<his>> outfit.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> finishes bringing the food to the tables, then comes back behind the counter.
	"They just ordered their food," <<he>> says, glancing down at <<his>> outfit. "Nobody said anything about it. I thought someone would."
	<<npcincr Robin trauma -4>><<llrtrauma>>
<<else>>
	Robin brings food and drinks to the tables in <<his>> new outfit. Most customers are more interested in their orders than in what <<hes>> wearing.
	<br><br>
	When <<he>> returns to the counter, <<he>> looks pleased. "A woman asked me where the toilets were. She asked <i>me</i> because I looked like someone who worked here."
	<<npcincr Robin dom 2>><<gdom>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Outfit Debut 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Outfit Debut 2
<<effects>>
Sam walks past carrying a tray and stops beside Robin for a second.
"Suits you," <<nnpc_he "Sam">> says, then continues towards the tables.
<br><br>
Robin watches <<nnpc_him "Sam">> leave. <<He>> does not answer, but a smile spreads across <<his>> face.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Outfit Regulars
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<if !$robinCafe.outfit>>
	Robin doesn't have anything of yours to wear.
	<br><br>
	<<robinOutfitReturn>>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
<<generates2>>
<<set $robinCafe.outfit.seen.regulars to true>>
There are more customers in the cafe than you usually see on a weekday.
Several of them look towards Robin while <<he>> moves between the tables.
<br><br>
Sam notices you looking around.
<br><br>
"Someone shared a photo of Robin in that outfit," <<nnpc_he "Sam">> says while entering an order into Old Betsy.
"People have been talking about it. I've already had four customers this week ask if the other staff can wear one too."
<br><br>
<<nnpc_He "Sam">> smiles as <<nnpc_he "Sam">> says it, though <<nnpc_he "Sam">> keeps glancing towards Robin to check how <<hes>> doing. <<robinOutfitLook>>
Robin takes an order across the café. On the way, <<he>> stops beside another table to ask if anyone needs another drink, then carries on with the food.
<br><br>
You notice that <<hes>> getting more comfortable talking to customers. <<He>> no longer waits beside every table while people decide what to say, so <<he>> can serve more of them.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Outfit Regulars 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Outfit Regulars 2
<<effects>>
<<person2>>A <<person>> sitting at the corner table raises a hand as Robin passes. "Can I get a photo with you?"
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<if !$robinCafe.outfit>>
	Robin doesn't have anything of yours to wear.
	<br><br>
	<<robinOutfitReturn>>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<person1>>Robin stops beside the table. <<He>> looks at the <<person2>><<person>>,
then down at <<his>> tray while <<he>> decides what to say.
<br><br>
You have seen Robin agree to requests before because <<he>> was too nervous to refuse.
This time, <<he>> takes a few seconds before answering.
<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 70>>
	"No, thanks. What would you like to order?"
	<br><br>
	The <<person2>><<person>> accepts the answer and gives <<him>> an order instead.
	<<person1>>Later, Robin comes back to the counter and looks towards you.
	<br><br>
	"I can say no to that. Sam told me I don't have to let customers take photos just because they ask."
	<<He>> gives a small smile. "I think I'm getting better at remembering that." <<npcincr Robin dom 3>><<ggdom>>
<<elseif $robinCafe.outfit.sexy>>
	"...Alright," <<he>> says after a short pause. "But only my face and the top of the outfit. Nothing below my waist."
	Robin shows the customer where the photograph should end by placing a hand across <<his>> waist.
	<br><br>
	The <<person2>><<person>> agrees. Robin holds <<his>> tray in front of <<his>> waist while the customer takes the photograph, then returns to the counter. <<His>> cheeks are red, but <<hes>> smiling.
	<<npcincr Robin lust 3>><<npcincr Robin dom 1>><<gglust>><<gdom>>
<<else>>
	"Alright," <<he>> says, "but you have to order something first."
	<br><br>
	The <<person2>><<person>> laughs, then gives <<him>> an order before taking the photograph.
	<br><br>
	When Robin returns to the counter, <<he>> shows you the money from the order with a small smile.
	"I didn't think they'd agree to that."<<npcincr Robin dom 2>><<ggdom>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Outfit Regulars 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Outfit Regulars 3
<<effects>>
<<person1>>The cafe becomes quieter after several customers leave.
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<if !$robinCafe.outfit>>
	Robin doesn't have anything of yours to wear.
	<br><br>
	<<robinOutfitReturn>>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
When the café becomes less busy, Robin comes back to the counter and takes some coins from <<his>> pocket.
<br><br>
"Customers have been giving me extra money after they pay," <<he>> says. "Sam says we can keep that money for ourselves."
<br><br>
<<He>> puts the money away, then looks down at the <<= $robinCafe.outfit.name>>
and smooths part of the fabric with <<his>> hand.
<br><br>
"I thought I'd feel embarrassed wearing this in front of everyone," <<he>> says. "But I don't feel as embarrassed anymore."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>> <br>

:: Robin Stand Haggle Firm
<<robinStandLocation $robinStandVenue>><<effects>>
<<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
You step up beside Robin.
<<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"P-please pay for the extra drink," you say. "Robin can't give it away for free."
	<<case "shy">>
		"S-sorry, but Robin already told you the price," you say. "You need to pay for another cup."
	<<case "polite">>
		"Robin has already told you the price," you say. "Please pay if you still want another cup."
	<<case "confident">>
		"You heard Robin," you say. "Pay for the extra drink, or hand the cup back."
	<<case "bratty">>
		"You've argued long enough," you say. "Pay for it and let the next person order."
	<<case "docile">>
		"Please pay Robin for the extra drink," you say quietly. "There are other customers waiting."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"Robin has already told you the price," you say. "Please pay if you still want another cup."
	<<case "cruel">>
		"Stop wasting Robin's time," you say. "Either pay or get out of the way so someone else can order."
	<<default>>
		"The price hasn't changed," you say. "Pay for the extra drink, or give the cup back."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
The <<person2>><<person>> turns to look at the customers waiting behind <<him>>. A few are watching the argument, so <<he>> turns back, puts the money on the counter, and says, "Fine." Robin gives <<him>> the refill, and the customer walks away.
<<set $robinmoney += $robinStandVenue is "park" ? 2 : 1>>
<br><br>
<<endevent>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<if _robin.trauma gte 40>>
	Robin lowers <<his>> shoulders after the customer leaves. "I never know what to say to people like that. I know I should say no, but then I can't get the words out."
	<<ltrauma>><<trauma -3>>
<<else>>
	"I should have said that myself," Robin says as the customer leaves. <<He>> repeats your last sentence quietly, then nods to <<himself>>.
	<<npcincr Robin dom 1>><<gdom>>
<</if>>
<<run V.robinStand.skill = Math.min(ensureRobinStand().skill + 10, 1000)>>
<br><br>
<<robinStandOptions $robinStandVenue>>

:: Robin Stand Haggle Charm
<<robinStandLocation $robinStandVenue>><<effects>>
<<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
<<set $seductiondifficulty to 3000>>
<<seductioncheck>>
<<seductionskilluptext>>
<<seductionskilluse>>
<<promiscuity1>>
You lean on the counter beside the <<person2>><<person>>.
<<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"Robin's being nicer than I would be," you say with a nervous smile. "I might have asked you to pay double."
	<<case "shy">>
		"Y-you're lucky Robin is serving you," you say with a small smile. "I'd have charged double for all that arguing."
	<<case "polite">>
		"Robin is being kind to you," you say with a smile. "I would have charged double for the extra drink."
	<<case "confident">>
		"You're lucky Robin is serving you," you say with a smile. "I'd charge double after all that complaining."
	<<case "bratty">>
		"All that trouble over one drink?" you say with a grin. "I'd charge you double just for arguing."
	<<case "docile">>
		"Robin's being very kind," you say softly, trying to smile at the customer. "I would have asked for more money."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"Robin is being kind to you," you say with a smile. "I would have charged double for the extra drink."
	<<case "cruel">>
		"You've made quite a fuss over one drink," you say with a smile. "I'd make you pay twice as much."
	<<default>>
		"Robin's nicer than me," you say, smiling. "I'd have charged you double for arguing."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<if $seductionrating gte $seductionrequired>>
	Your comment makes the customer laugh. <<He>> puts more money on the counter than the drink costs, then stays there to drink and keeps looking at you instead of walking away.
	<<set _tip to 3 + Math.round(robinStandCrowdPull())>>
	<span class="green">Robin takes £<<print _tip>>.</span><<set $robinmoney += _tip>>
	<<famebusiness 1>>
	<br><br>
	<<person1>>Robin laughs. "That's not fair. You didn't even argue with <<person2>><<him>>."
	<<endevent>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<else>>
	The <<person2>><<person>> looks annoyed instead of laughing. Before either of you can ask for the money again, <<he>> takes the refilled cup from Robin's hand and walks away without paying.
	<<gstress>><<stress 6>>
	<br><br>
	<<endevent>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
	Robin looks at your expression. "It's one cup," <<he>> says quickly. "Honestly. It's one cup."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinStandOptions $robinStandVenue>>

:: Robin Stand Haggle Robin
