<<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinStand()>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		"M-maybe we can still sell what's left," you say. "Some people might not notice anything wrong."
	<<case "shy">>
		"We could serve the drinks we still have," you suggest quietly. "Maybe the customers won't notice."
	<<case "polite">>
		"We can still serve what's left," you say. "It might help us get some of the lost money back."
	<<case "confident">>
		"Sell the drinks that are left," you say. "We can still get some of the money back."
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Just sell it," you say. "They've already waited this long. They can complain after they pay."
	<<case "docile">>
		"We could sell what's left," you say softly. "At least it would bring in some money."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"We can still serve what's left," you say. "It might help us get some of the lost money back."
	<<case "cruel">>
		"Sell the rest anyway," you say. "Let them find out how bad it is after they've paid."
	<<default>>
		"Let's sell what's left," you say. "Most of the customers probably won't notice until they drink it."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<if _robin.trauma gte 40>>
	Robin looks down at the remaining drink, then starts filling cups as you asked. <<He>> keeps <<his>> eyes on the cups instead of looking at the customers or at you, even when someone speaks to <<him>>.
	<<npcincr Robin trauma 2>>
<<else>>
	"I don't think we should—" Robin begins, but stops when <<he>> sees how many people are still waiting. <<He>> fills the remaining cups and hands them out.
	<br><br>
	Several customers take a drink and immediately complain. Some say there isn't enough flavour, while others find bits of unmixed ingredients in their cups.
	<<npcincr Robin love -1>><<llove>>
